From: Ruhan <35257374+RuhanSA079@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] radxa-cm3-io: fiq-debugger console at 115200 baud

The Radxa CM3 IO's board dts (added by the previous patch) does not
carry its own /chosen or serial console setup; it inherits both from
the shared rk3568-linux.dtsi, which puts the debug console on the
Rockchip fiq-debugger driver (ttyFIQ0) at a non-standard 1500000
baud. Switch it to the standard 115200 so it matches the U-Boot
console. Unlike a plain 8250 UART, ttyFIQ0's baud is fixed by this
"rockchip,baudrate" property, not by the "console=" bootarg speed.

---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3568-linux.dtsi | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3568-linux.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3568-linux.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3568-linux.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3568-linux.dtsi
@@ -22,7 +22,7 @@
 		rockchip,wake-irq = <0>;
 		/* If enable uart uses irq instead of fiq */
 		rockchip,irq-mode-enable = <1>;
-		rockchip,baudrate = <1500000>;  /* Only 115200 and 1500000 */
+		rockchip,baudrate = <115200>;  /* Only 115200 and 1500000 */
 		interrupts = <GIC_SPI 252 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW>;
 		pinctrl-names = "default";
 		pinctrl-0 = <&uart2m0_xfer>;
--
